VCSU AI Institute – Sample Artifact: T3.1 Assessment Rubric

Module T3.1 – Designing AI-Assisted Formative Assessments

This sample rubric demonstrates how AI can help create clear, standards-aligned assessment criteria. Upload this file into the Module T3.1 simulator to see a demonstration AI response.

SAMPLE FORMATIVE ASSESSMENT RUBRIC:

Assignment: Persuasive Essay | Grade 8 | ELA Standards: W.8.1

Criteria | 4 – Exceeds | 3 – Meets | 2 – Approaching | 1 – Beginning
Claim & Evidence | Clear claim with 3+ AI-verified sources | Clear claim with 2 sources | Claim present, 1 source | No clear claim
Organization | Logical flow, strong transitions | Organized with some transitions | Some organization | Disorganized
Reasoning | Sophisticated analysis | Sound reasoning | Basic reasoning | Limited reasoning
Conventions | Error-free, varied sentences | Few errors | Several errors | Many errors

AI Assistance Used:
- AI generated initial criteria descriptions
- Teacher refined based on student needs
- AI suggested examples for each level

Feedback Protocol: AI provides immediate written feedback; teacher conferences for level 1-2 students.

This file is a training artifact for the VCSU AI Institute for Teaching and Learning.
